From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] media: apple: avd: keep working with firmware without a
 config block

Asahi's "media: apple: avd: Announce only codecs the firmware supports"
(7.2.15) reads the codec list from a config block in the firmware and
fails the probe when there is none. Firmware built from avd-fw before
that block existed, which is what a machine that took it from the
pre-0.2 sources has, then leaves the machine with no decoder at all.
Nothing else in this driver's interface to the firmware changed.

Fall back to the SoC's list with a warning, as the driver did before
for firmware without the older CODECS: tail.

Tested: build only (7.2.15). Not run on hardware yet.
---
 avd-drv.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/avd-drv.c b/avd-drv.c
index 17814f5..e560bee 100644
--- a/avd-drv.c
+++ b/avd-drv.c
@@ -745,8 +745,11 @@ static int avd_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		u32 fw_caps = get_unaligned_le32(avd->fw->data + codec_offset);
 		avd->capabilities = fw_caps & avd->variant->capabilities;
 	} else {
-		dev_err(avd->dev, "Too old or incompatible firmware without config\n");
-		return -EINVAL;
+		/* avd-fw from before the config block: as Asahi's driver did until
+		 * 7.2.15, trust the SoC's list.
+		 */
+		dev_warn(avd->dev, "Firmware without config block, assuming the SoC's codecs\n");
+		avd->capabilities = avd->variant->capabilities;
 	}
 
 	ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(avd->dev,
